# The unrecognised-mode run in templates/minimal-vulkan-ofx/test/run-tests.bat,
# Windows 11 + RTX 3060 + Vulkan 1.4.357, 2026-11-27 (excerpt of the runner's
# 1079-line log, which stays in .validation/).
#
# What this proves, and what it is for: OFXPLUGIN_VULKAN_MODE=gpux is a word
# VulkanMode.h does not know. The policy test (vulkan_mode_test) already asserts
# that the parser reports it as unrecognised; nothing asserted that the decision
# reaches a user, which is the half that makes a typo harmless-or-not. The runner
# sets the variable, renders one frame, and asks the harness for the Device
# parameter with --label-contains, so the run fails if the label does not carry
# the sentence. Two checks, both in this block: the label's value and the
# substring, at check 29/30 on the first render and 76/77 on the second.
#
# The label is the device's, because an unrecognised word reads as auto and this
# machine has a device: `NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3060 (Vulkan 1.4.357, queue family 0,
# 4294967040 px per dispatch); OFXPLUGIN_VULKAN_MODE='gpux' is not auto, cpu or
# gpu`. On a machine with no device the same sentence arrives on the CPU label
# (`cpuLabel()` appends it too), so the run is not a device-only pass.
#
# Counts: this run is 94 checks, the same shape as the forced-CPU run; the
# template's total is 899, the tree's 3,017.

